   <collaboration id="Collaboration_f3e4c697-61a1-45ec-9aca-9e00dff58e95"
                   name="CSP-BPMN-L2-002 - Process Amendment and Cancellation"
                   isClosed="false">
      <documentation><![CDATA[Traceability: CSP-PR-002; CSP-LC-001-004; CSP-SM-001-007.
 
Purpose: Represent the assumed current-state operational handling of amendment and cancellation lifecycle events for an existing FX Forward trade.
 
The process begins when an AMEND or CANCEL event is available for downstream processing. It covers lifecycle and version validation, assessment of affected valuation, accounting and settlement states, controlled preparation and submission to SYS-FAP, processing-result reconciliation, resulting-state verification, operational tracking and exception recovery.
 
The process ends with either confirmed successful lifecycle completion or a documented unsuccessful exception outcome with a recorded status, assigned owner, supporting evidence and required next action. 
 
Upstream trade execution and event recording in SYS-TBS, detailed FAP ledger logic, external payment execution, internal NAV calculation and target-state automation are outside scope.
 
Evidence status: Current-state case-study assumption.]]></documentation>
